    "text": "<p>Non-metal oxides are generally acidic in nature.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></math> Acidic</p><p>Metal oxides are generally basic&nbsp;in nature</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;Basic</p><p>Amphoteric oxides reacts with both acids and bases.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Al</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></math> Amphoteric.</p><p>Some non-metal oxides don&#39;t react with both acids and bases they are neutral in nature.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;Netural</p>"
